From 782b67a9d3bc3b89e6597da9be1bfc99f014ad2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 02:55:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Allow main-account UpCloud login and add plan/disk/backup/IP
 management

The connect flow now accepts the main UpCloud account's own username and
password (with a note on the API's own "Permit API connections" and
2FA-off requirements) instead of insisting on a separate API sub-account.

Also closes the biggest remaining gaps toward "everything the UpCloud
site can do": changing a server's plan (gated on the server being
stopped, matching UpCloud's own requirement), full disk management
(attach/resize/detach/delete), disk backups (create/list/restore/delete),
and public IP management (add/remove) on the server detail screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
